Add support for a `!docs` modifier that works with the `!file` modifier to only
import the first comment,  of a file. Use regular expressions to match common
programming languages.

Also include support for python triple double quotes and front matter.

Ignore shebangs at the start of files should be ignored when looking for documentation.

Examples:

Source:
``` js
#!/usr/bin/env bun
/**
 * File documentation here
 */

const someConst=1;

export const someLongFunction=()=>{
    // lots of lines of code
}
```

Imported value:
``` js
#!/usr/bin/env bun
/**
 * File documentation here
 */
```


If documentation is not found at the start of a file the first 1500 characters should be imported

A file truncated XML tag should be inserted at the end of the imported content if the entire file content.
is not imported and FILE_CONTENT blocks should also
include a truncated boolean attribute and the system prompt for code blocks should document the behavior

Truncation example:
<FILE_CONTENT name="control-center.md" target-output-path="../context/control-center.md" truncated>
``` md
# Controls center
... more content here

<FILE_CONTENT_TRUNCATION/>
```
</FILE_CONTENT>


